ed, Neglected, or Exploited: Based upon the information gathered during the investigation, sufficient evidence was available to support neglectful supervision due to a child being left in the vehicle unattended.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026645005","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5605-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003","date":"2025-10-03","original_code":"746.5605(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-01-07","finding":"AP Safety Precautions for Loading and Unloading Children - No Child Unattended: Based upon the information obtained during the investigation, sufficient evidence was available to support, the driver failed to follow the facilities procedures regarding safety precautions for loading and unloading children which resulted in a child being left in the center's vehicle unattended.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026654167","violation_type_title":"AP Safety Precautions for Loading and Unloading Children - No Child Unattended (26 TAC §746.5605(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5617-a-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003","date":"2025-10-03","original_code":"746.5617(a)(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-01-07","finding":"Required Equipment in Vehicles - List of Children: Based on the information provided, bus logs were not documented for children transported from September 1- September 28, 2025.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026651977","violation_type_title":"Required Equipment in Vehicles - List of Children (26 TAC §746.5617(a)(1))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-307-b-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003","date":"2025-10-03","original_code":"746.307(b)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-12-23","finding":"Parental Communication - Situation that Placed a Child at Risk: Based on the information obtained, a parent was not notified of an incident that placed their child at risk. A child was left unsupervised on the transportation vehicle at 3:58PM and was not retrieved until 4:33PM. Based on the information obtained, the parent was not notified until pick-up at 5:45PM. The operation failed to notify the parents immediately of a serious incident directly involving their child.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026652008","violation_type_title":"Parental Communication - Situation that Placed a Child at Risk (26 TAC §746.307(b)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5605-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20251003","date":"2025-10-03","original_code":"746.5605(3)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-01-07","finding":"Safety Precautions for Loading and Unloading Children - Account for All Children: Based upon the information gathered during the investigation, evidence was available to support the safety precautions for unloading children was not followed. Two staff conducting transportation services did not account for all children present on the vehicle. As a result, a child was left in the van unattended for approximately 30-40 minutes.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026645004","violation_type_title":"Safety Precautions for Loading and Unloading Children - Account for All Children (26 TAC §746.5605(3))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1485614-i20250925","date":"2025-0